278
00:07:53,171 --> 00:07:54,359
from a bygone decade.

279
00:07:54,989 --> 00:07:56,885
They are structural decisions about

280
00:07:56,885 --> 00:07:58,475
pacing and patience, and every

281
00:07:58,475 --> 00:07:59,661
one of them requires a

282
00:07:59,661 --> 00:08:01,197
show, and a network standing

283
00:08:01,197 --> 00:08:02,599
behind it, willing to let

284
00:08:02,599 --> 00:08:03,520
a story take its

285
00:08:03,520 --> 00:08:04,440
time to pay off.

286
00:08:05,239 --> 00:08:07,044
Twin Peaks demonstrates exactly what

287
00:08:07,044 --> 00:08:08,566
happens when that patience gets

288
00:08:08,566 --> 00:08:09,915
overridden from the outside

289
00:08:09,915 --> 00:08:10,869
for a ratings sweep.

290
00:08:10,879 --> 00:08:11,755
E R and N Y

291
00:08:11,755 --> 00:08:13,506
P D Blue show what

292
00:08:13,506 --> 00:08:17,258
patience built instead, when nobody

